cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Traffic Vision Senegal: measuring urban mobility policies from video, with honest uncertainty"
abstract: >
  Open-source framework that turns existing traffic video into evidence on
  mobility rules in African cities. Rules are described in measure registries
  (reserved lanes, bans on a class, banned movements, service frequencies,
  closures) and local vehicles in context profiles; any Ultralytics detector,
  closed or open vocabulary, counts road users with ByteTrack; the effect of
  a rule is estimated by a prediction-powered difference-in-differences that
  corrects the network's errors with a few hand-counted windows per
  recording and accounts for autocorrelated traffic. Worked example: the
  Dakar 2026 Youth Olympic Games; registries for the Dakar BRT corridor, the
  Lagos okada ban and the Kigali car-free days.
authors:
